<title>INDIA: Indian soy prices firm on processing plants demand.</title>
<headline>Indian soy prices firm on processing plants demand.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices firmed on good demand from processing plants on Monday, gaining by 50-100 rupees per tonne, dealers said.</p>
<p>Soyoil solvent rose by 200 rupees and soyoil refined was up by 400 rupees on strong undertone.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were firm on good export demand. Soymeal yellow was $290 per tonne for current season and was $272-275 per tonne for new November - December 1996 delivery season.</p>
<p>Rapeseed extraction was $121 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,150-4,200 rupees FOR Bedibunder and 4,100-4,150 FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
